A||N||2||FIL||What's up with my Radio?||||8||
Z||000000||FIL||10-20-2001||11:47 AM||||Can someone help me on this one?...I have this 87GT that has an electrical problem.  Nothing major, but annoying!!  Everytime I open the door and the domelight comes on, my radio resets and goes back to 10 o'clock.  Has anyone had this happen to them and if so what was the fix?  The only solution I have it to go in and out of the car via "Dukes of Hazard" style.  Only one problem with that idea, I don't want to always slide over the hood of my car to get me into the mood of getting in it.||||reg||8
Z||000001||NorthernFiero||10-20-2001||12:26 PM|||| Yes, I have the same problem in my 87SE how do you fix it? but mine is when i hit the lighter it chages the clock to 10 and turns the lights in the foot wells on. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000002||theogre||10-20-2001||12:50 PM||||You may need the wire diagrams for the car.<P>You'll love this one...<P>The dome light is run from the CTSY/LID fuse. Most people know that.<P>However, the foot lights are run by the BAT fuse... Yup... Same one that holds radio presets and runs the lighter.<P>Somewhere on those circuits is a problem. It could be a simple as one of the fuses fried.<P>The radio is probably getting standby power sneaking thru the foot light filaments. When the lighter is pressed or the door pins activated the radio can't get standby power and resets.<P>Could be in that one case that the lighter is bad. May be drawing too much power due to partial short. this would cause the BAT fuse to keep frying. Lighter sockets collect allot of trash. Fiero's more so due to location.<P>The lighter, like most of them in U.S. cars, is a Casco and parts are readily available.<P>The Fiero lighter knob can be screwed onto a new heater, the socket can be repared with standard Casco parts but you'll need to reuse some of the Fiero's parts. (Namely the outter sleeve and light plus the terminal that screws on the base.)<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">   <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-20-2001).]||||reg||1
